{"_id":"68a736218ec3d8323af18f15","nodeId":"ImS1FqVicQImMw-y1ze7y","roadmapSlug":"ios","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:12.170Z","description":"# User Defaults\n\nUser Defaults is a simple key-value store for persisting lightweight user preferences and settings across app launches. It stores basic types like strings, numbers, booleans, and dates in a plist file. User Defaults is not suitable for sensitive or large data and is intended only for small configuration values.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"UserDefaults","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/userdefaults","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf86e6"},{"type":"article","title":"Reading and Writing basics: UserDefaults","url":"https://www.hackingwithswift.com/read/12/2/reading-and-writing-basics-userdefaults","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf86e7"},{"type":"video","title":"Reading and Writing basics: UserDefaults","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WHKLXI8baJk&t=1s","_id":"6a7f4a98cb44947debcf86e8"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:04:24.838Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ios/content/ImS1FqVicQImMw-y1ze7y.md"}